Perception note for this scene: object poses come from a computer-vision pipeline (OpenCV) on an overhead RGB-D camera, with a front camera as backup, not from the simulator. Typical error is a few millimetres, worse when an object is partly hidden. An object that neither camera can see (for example under the gripper or under another object) is missing from observe()['objects'], and get_pose() raises LookupError for it: move the gripper out of the way and look again. Object mass, friction and grip force also vary between episodes.

Task: Put the red cube into the red tray and the blue cube into the blue tray.

